        <h2>The Engineering Behind EV Charger Reliability in Issaquah Highlands</h2>
        <p>
          Electric vehicle supply equipment is fundamentally different from virtually any other electrical appliance in a modern home. Unlike a standard electric clothes dryer or air conditioning condenser that cycles on and off as temperatures fluctuate, a Level 2 EV charging station pulls high continuous current for six, eight, or even ten consecutive hours. Under the National Electrical Code (NEC Article 625), an electric vehicle circuit must be treated as a continuous load, meaning the branch circuit conductors and overcurrent protection devices must be sized at 125% of the continuous draw.
        </p>

        <figure class="seo-location-figure" style="margin-block: 2.25rem; text-align: center;">
