          <li><strong>Comprehensive Manufacturer Experience:</strong> Certified familiarity across Tesla Wall Connectors, ChargePoint Home Flex, Wallbox, Autel, Emporia, Grizzl-E, and JuiceBox hardware.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Our Step-by-Step Diagnostic and Repair Protocol</h2>
        <p>
          When you contact our dispatch team regarding an EVSE malfunction in Issaquah Highlands, we follow a meticulous four-stage service procedure:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Initial Technical Consultation:</strong> We identify your EV model, charger hardware, and specific error indications (such as red LED flash counts or breaker trip patterns) to equip our service vehicles with the required replacement components.</li>
          <li><strong>On-Site Electrical Inspection:</strong> Upon arrival, our electrician conducts non-invasive infrared thermal scans, tests split-phase voltage stability at your panel, measures branch circuit loop impedance, and tests grounding electrode resistance.</li>
          <li><strong>Precision Hardware Repair:</strong> Defective breakers, melted receptacles, damaged cables, or loose terminal blocks are repaired or replaced using code-compliant materials torqued to manufacturer specifications.</li>
          <li><strong>Live-Load Commissioning:</strong> We connect diagnostic test equipment or your vehicle to initiate a live charging cycle, monitoring voltage drop, amperage stability, and thermal dissipation under continuous full-load operating conditions.</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>Straight-Forward Assessment Standards</h2>
        <p>
          Electrical troubleshooting requires clarity and technical honesty. We conduct all on-site diagnostics with complete transparency. Our technicians explain every step of the testing process, identify the physical components causing failure, and outline the precise corrective actions necessary to restore safe, uninterrupted charging to your Issaquah Highlands home.
